        "title": "Deep Copy (JSON trick)",
        "explanation": "First, `JSON.stringify` converts the object to a string, then `JSON.parse` recreates it as a new object.\nIn this process, all nested structures are serialized and then rebuilt from scratch, resulting in a completely independent copy.\n\n**Analogy**: It's like converting a building into blueprints, shipping them to the other side of the world, and constructing a brand-new building with identical materials.\nA perfect clone.",
        "keyInsight": "Deep copy = all levels copied, completely independent",
